# An ESP32-S3 (four 32-bit slots on one line) lists every layout and greys the ones it cannot carry, with the
# reason beside them: a tap on a greyed one changes nothing, a layout it carries with a limit is taken. Preview
# only: no board on the bench has these capabilities, so a run with --board refuses it at the profile.
board s3-spi-320x240
display 1024 600
scene lyrics

tap "Preferences"
expect shown "Speaker layout"
expect pref speaker-layout = 2.0
expect text "5.1 needs 6 slots"

tap "5.1"
expect pref speaker-layout = 2.0

tap "2.1"
expect pref speaker-layout = 2.1

tap "2.0"
expect pref speaker-layout = 2.0
